nual points, rising from 24% in 2024 to 26% in 2025 and 27% in 2026. That's too thin to say much beyond a slight drift up.\n- **Skew:** Flat, so there's no extra cost for calls or puts.\n- **Term structure:** Nearly flat, at 26% for Jan-2027, 27% for Jan-2028 and 27.5% for Jan-2029. Longer expiries cost only slightly more vol, so there's no obvious expiry to favour.\n\nPricing alone doesn't make these attractive. Whether to add depends on your view of VLTX's fundamentals, mainly utility order intake and data-centre demand, which other nodes are covering. Data-centre grid connection requests are expected to grow 9% in 2027, slower than in 2026. If you do buy, the Jan-2028 expiry is a reasonable middle choice on vol cost.\n\nI didn't have the underlying price, strikes or option premiums, so I couldn't check realized volatility or the premium itself. This is a view on implied volatility only.","ttft_ms":2527,"type":"result","duration_ms":24190,"uuid":"86ff119f-4ea2-4a2a-b601-4c44b68c61e8","ttft_stream_ms":1761,"time_to_request_ms":136,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":14,"system_prompt":8,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":7,"input_attachments":18,"input_hooks":4,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":7,"init_message":13,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":8,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":4,"request_announcements":18,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":8,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":6,"request_build":10},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":80,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":69,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":188,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":114,"process_rss_mib_result":197,"process_anon_mib_result":116,"process_peak_rss_mib":199,"process_cpu_ms_turn":518,"process_wall_ms_turn":24184,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":55,"process_wall_ms_streaming":1343,"main_stream_count":3,"main_stream_event_count":150,"